        "Examiners in {S} test the numbers: resting potential minus 70 millivolts, fasting glucose 3.9 to 5.5 mmol per litre, cranial nerve count, and which lobe handles vision, the occipital. They also set the hypothalamus-pituitary order, asking where antidiuretic hormone is made, in the hypothalamus, and where it is released, from the posterior pituitary. Write both halves of such answers or forfeit half the credit.",
