        "Safe administration rests on the five rights: right patient, right drug, right dose, right route, right time. Each right is a checkpoint, confirm identity by name and record number, read the label twice, recalculate the dose, confirm the route, respect the interval. Three duties complete the ritual: check allergies, check expiry, document at once. Most medication errors are failures of these simple checks rather than of knowledge, which is why the checklist is recited on every ward round of {S}.",
