        "Deterioration announces itself as a trend: rising pulse and respiratory rate, falling blood pressure and saturation, falling consciousness, falling urine output. Early warning charts score these so that a climbing total over hours rings the alarm before collapse. The septic patient shows fever or abnormally low temperature, fast breathing, fast weak pulse and confusion. Spotting deterioration is a team skill, and the most junior nurse counting respiratory rates honestly saves more lives than any monitor, the culture {S} exists to build.",
